let's look at a third example

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.530
of choosing the right chart type.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:46.340
So here you have the example of a P and L.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.800
So profit and loss statement of a company,

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.220
one of the three key financial statements

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:52.620
the companies need to produce.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.010
So let's imagine you
would want to visualize

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:58.960
this P and L in a chart, which
one would you like to choose?

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.480
And here again, pause a moment.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:01.313
Think about this.

00:11:01.313 --> 00:11:03.220
Maybe this is less trivial, less clear

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:06.250
because indeed one chart
type that is extensively used

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.110
in consulting that is very well suited

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:10.700
also to visualize things like P and Ls

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.240
are the waterfall charts.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.120
So what we have here is
the data entry window

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:15.400
of think-cell, you can see that

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:16.773
I already copied in all the numbers.

00:11:16.773 --> 00:11:18.790
The letter E stands for equals.

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:20.150
Some things (indistinct) can help you

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:23.110
to automatically calculate
totals and sub-totals.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:25.270
So no need to do this manually anymore.

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:27.240
Think-cell will do the
calculations for you

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.420
and provide you with the correct results.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.850
And also notice how you can
stack waterfall segments

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:34.220
just by writing the
numbers under each other

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:36.180
here in the column for the personnel cost.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.810
And indeed, this is the resize,.

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:40.320
this is what the waterfall
chart will look like

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:41.870
but now you're already seeing a problem.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:44.340
And this is because all
the numbers are entered

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:45.530
in million, right?

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.040
So the numbers are quite long.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.800
This is surely not how you
would want them to look like.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:50.690
So what do you do now?

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:53.080
Do you need to now go back
to the data entry mask

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:55.250
and change all the numbers or the Excel,

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.771
by the way, you can also
integrate things that are in Excel

00:11:57.771 --> 00:11:59.830
to automatically update charts like this.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:00.690
Well, of course not

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.610
because one of the many very handy things

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.910
and functionalities is that
just with a couple of clicks,

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:08.450
you can really transport
all these numbers.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.497
And for instance, round them to millions

00:12:10.497 --> 00:12:13.630
as I'm doing right here just
with a couple of clicks,

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:14.760
you have really the chart bar

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.800
exactly the way that you want it to look.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:19.970
So now last but not least, let's
look at some typical errors

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.110
that people do when they create charts.

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.920
And I think one of the main problems is

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.790
if you just use the
built-in PowerPoint charts,

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:30.140
so not use the think-cell
charts, then often these charts

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.350
come already pre-configured
with some problem.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.130
So all the charts you see right here

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.120
are design templates that
are suggested layouts,

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:40.550
suggested designs within PowerPoint.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.140
So here you see charts
with these glossy effects,

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:45.750
with shadows, with 3D effects,

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.910
with these real shaded backgrounds.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.000
So now we could look into
this in much more detail

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.481
but I hope that you agree just
at the first look and feel,

00:12:52.481 --> 00:12:55.500
that these charts don't
really look professional.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.350
So let's just look here at this
profitability surface chart

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:01.517
which again is one of the
suggested templates by PowerPoint.

00:13:01.517 --> 00:13:04.202
how this looks, I mean
it's virtually impossible

00:13:04.202 --> 00:13:07.900
to get really any insight,
any message out of this chart

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:10.560
at all, just to distill any
number out of it at all.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.090
So you should really avoid
all layouts like this.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:15.730
I think we now extensively
already talked about formatting.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.700
I wanna leave you with
one last piece of advice

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.740
because this is something
that I often also see

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:21.850
done wrongly and this is in general

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:24.820
trying to avoid having
too many different charts,

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.262
too many different messages on one slide.

00:13:27.262 --> 00:13:29.590
There is the basic rule of thumb

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:32.192
which says, one message per slide.

00:13:32.192 --> 00:13:35.890
Really try to stick to
one search per slide.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:38.900
This usually makes the whole
storytelling much easier,

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:42.130
helps you to create more to
the point, nicely formatted,

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:45.940
nicely layout pages, several
charts on one page can be okay

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:48.470
but only if you really
need all these charts

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.630
next to each other, to really
get the one message out

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:54.510
that you want to share,
otherwise rather split it up

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:56.210
and show them on different pages.

